      "title": "The limiting sum of a geometric series",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "chs2020e1-q9",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "stem": "A geometric series \\(1-\\frac1x+\\frac{1}{x^2}-\\frac{1}{x^3}+\\dots\\) has limiting sum \\(S\\).\nFor what values of \\(x\\) is \\(S\\lt 1\\)?",
          "hint": "First require |r| < 1, then compare S = x/(x + 1) with 1.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "First term \\(a=1\\), ratio \\(r=-\\frac1x\\). A limiting sum exists only if \\(|r|\\lt1\\).",
              "work": "\\(\\left|\\frac1x\\right|\\lt1\\ \\Rightarrow\\ |x|\\gt1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Limiting sum.",
              "work": "\\(S=\\frac{a}{1-r}=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac1x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "For \\(x\\gt1\\): \\(\\frac{x}{x+1}\\lt1\\) because the numerator is smaller than the denominator.",
              "work": "\\(x=2:\\ S=\\tfrac23\\lt1\\ \\checkmark\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "For \\(x\\lt-1\\): both \\(x\\) and \\(x+1\\) are negative and \\(|x|\\gt|x+1|\\), so \\(S\\gt1\\).",
              "work": "\\(x=-2:\\ S=\\frac{-2}{-1}=2\\gt1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "So \\(S\\lt1\\) exactly when \\(x\\gt1\\): option D."
            }
          ],
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Caringbah 2020 3U Trials & Solutions",
            "school": "Caringbah High School",
            "year": 2020,
            "number": "9"
          },
          "options": [
            "\\(x\\gt -1\\)",
            "\\(x\\gt -1,\\ x\\neq0\\)",
            "\\(x\\gt 0\\)",
            "\\(x\\gt 1\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "has limiting sum",
              "note": "A limiting sum needs |r| = |1/x| < 1, so |x| > 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
